body:
I think I might have found the root cause of this hang. 

`AbstractProcessWorkerExecutorService.notifyQueueRunnables()` is called when an `AbstractProcessWorkerExecutorService` is stopped (which happens when the deployment on the node is stopped):
```
public synchronized void notifyQueueRunnables() {
    assert isShutdown() : "Queue runnables should only be drained and notified after the worker is shutdown";

    if (queue.isEmpty() == false) {
        logger.warn(
            format("[%s] notifying [%d] queued requests that have not been processed before shutdown", processName, queue.size())
        );

        List<Runnable> notExecuted = new ArrayList<>();
        queue.drainTo(notExecuted);

        String msg = "unable to process as " + processName + " worker service has shutdown";
        Exception ex = error.get();
        for (Runnable runnable : notExecuted) {
            if (runnable instanceof AbstractRunnable ar) {
                if (ex != null) {
                    ar.onFailure(ex);
                } else {
                    ar.onRejection(new EsRejectedExecutionException(msg, true));
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```
For each `Runnable` in `queue`, if it is an `AbstractRunnable`, either `onFailure()` or `onRejection()` is called. However, when performing inference as part of reindex, the `Runnable` added to `queue` in `PriorityProcessWorkerExecutorService.executeWithPriority()` is an `OrderedRunnable` wrapping the `AbstractRunnable` `command`:
```
queue.offer(new OrderedRunnable(priority, tieBreaker, contextHolder.preserveContext(command)));
```
 Since `OrderedRunnable` is not an `AbstractRunnable`, this results in `notifyQueueRunnables()` not calling `onFailure()` or `onRejection()` for the underlying `AbstractRunnable`, preventing it from completing.

I modified `notifyQueueRunnables()` to unwrap the `AbstractRunnable` and call `onFailure()` or `onRejection()`:
```
if (runnable instanceof AbstractRunnable ar) {
    if (ex != null) {
        ar.onFailure(ex);
    } else {
        ar.onRejection(new EsRejectedExecutionException(msg, true));
    }
} else {
    if (runnable instanceof PriorityProcessWorkerExecutorService.OrderedRunnable or) {
        if (or.runnable() instanceof WrappedRunnable wrappedRunnable) {
            if (wrappedRunnable.unwrap() instanceof AbstractRunnable ar) {
                if (ex != null) {
                    ar.onFailure(ex);
                } else {
                    ar.onRejection(new EsRejectedExecutionException(msg, true));
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```
with this change, the reindex task completes with failures rather than hangs:
```
"failures": [
  {
    "index": "dest-index",
    "id": "j5qjoZkBukYLSzk4zqd5",
    "cause": {
      "type": "inference_exception",
      "reason": "Exception when running inference id [test] on field [infer_field]",
      "caused_by": {
        "type": "status_exception",
        "reason": "Error in inference process: [inference canceled as process is stopping]"
      }
    },
    "status": 409
  },
...
```
